THE FINDING, stated as the invariant it violates. SPEC §3.2 requires the tmux socket and its custody chain to be owner-only. The custody predicate must therefore refuse **any** permission bit outside the owner triplet. The rev1 tests witness only the modes 0600 (admit) and 0644 (refuse). So the rule is pinned along one axis: a narrowing that ignores the other-bits (`perm&0o077` → `perm&0o070`) survived twice, and under it a world-connectable 0606 or 0602 socket passes custody at `ServerProber.Probe`, `ServerSpawner.Spawn` and `Lifecycle.Execute`. The reviewer's 0606 vector is evidence that the invariant is currently unpinned. It is not the work item. Fixing that one mode would leave the next bit open for the next round.

WHAT TO DELIVER.
(1) **A bit census, not more rows.** Each gate in `checkCustodySocket` and in the ancestor/root walk admits or refuses on some mask. For each gate × each of the six non-owner bits individually (0o040, 0o020, 0o010, 0o004, 0o002, 0o001), commit a row driving a mode with exactly that bit added to the admitted baseline. Drive each row through ALL THREE production entries (Probe, Spawn, Execute), and cover each path-component class the gate applies to: socket leaf, runtime `tmux` dir, ancestors, root. Where SPEC §3.2 deliberately admits a bit on a component class (for example, a sticky or group bit on a system ancestor), cite the spec line and record the cell `admitted-by-spec`. Assert the literal spec token (`tmux_unsafe_socket_path`) and the message, not a production constant. Assert zero Dial, zero spawn and zero dispatch. Rows can be table-driven, but every cell must be a named subtest so a kill is attributable.
(2) **Mask narrowings as harness mutants.** For every gate, ship the mask narrowings that drop the group triplet, the other triplet, and each single bit. That is `0o077` → `0o070`, `0o007`, and each `0o077 &^ bit`, plus the analogous narrowings of any directory mask. Run each ALONE against the tmuxserver and termbind packages and record the named killer. A NOT_APPLIED row counts as unmeasured. Include one applied, line-count-preserving neutral control.
(3) **Census table** in the conformance matrix and TRACEABILITY: gate × entry × component class × bit. Each cell holds a test name plus the mutant it kills, or `admitted-by-spec` with a citation, or a stated bound with an owner. Report the measured ratio.
(4) The registry needs no new acceptance case unless the spec clause set changes. If a test name that the registry or README cites changes, re-derive the digest and keep the README coverage pin equal to tracecheck.
(5) Re-run the importer outcome grid on base `14d636e` against the candidate, together with the full configured suite and `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...`. Update results, the conformance matrix and the evidence tar (under 1 MiB). Keep the checklist current, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-g0pcnt --role developer`.

